%N A400918 Number of symmetric two-rowed truncated monotone triangles of size n.
%C A400918 Two-rowed truncated monotone triangles of size n are in bijection with alternating sign matrices (ASMs) of size n such that for all i+j >= 8, M_{i,j} = 0. A two-rowed truncated monotone triangle is symmetric if the corresponding ASM is diagonally symmetric.
%C A400918 Let X be a two-rowed truncated monotone triangle. Entries of horizontal row k of X give the number of values > n-k in each diagonal row of the symmetric of X (see Example).
%H A400918 Ludovic Schwob, <a href="/A400918/a400918.txt">SageMath program</a>
%e A400918 The 7 two-rowed truncated monotone triangles of size 3 are the following:
%e A400918     1         2         2         3         3         1         2
%e A400918    2 1       3 1       3 2       3 1       3 2       3 1  <->  2 1
%e A400918   3 2       3 2       3 2       3 2       3 2       3 2       3 2
%e A400918 The first a(3) = 5 are symmetric, as the entries of horizontal row k give the number of values > n-k in each diagonal row.
